            <ArticleTitle>[Tiapride use in neoplasic algia (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>351-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The tiapride, usually prescribed in neurologic pathology, has been used in ENT carcinoma pain. On 30 cases of this study, we got 18 good results, that means a decrease of the pain in 60% cases. In all the cases, the tiapride was well tolerated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
